Fix readline_InputFifo return type to match readline_InputFunction.

Input.readline_Input is declared as returning `long`, but the FIFO
implementation returned `int`. On LP64 platforms (64-bit Linux, macOS)
this is undefined behaviour: the caller reads a 64-bit register whose
upper half is not guaranteed, so a negative error value can turn into a
large positive one. On Windows x64 (LLP64) `long` and `int` are both
32 bits, so the bug is latent there, but the compiler still warns and
the fix is harmless. Only the library (DLL / .so) build uses this code;
the standalone `mbrola` executable does not.

--- a/Parser/input_fifo.c
+++ b/Parser/input_fifo.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
    directly call with self for all functions, except Close
 */

-static int readline_InputFifo(Input* in, char *line, int size)
+static long readline_InputFifo(Input* in, char *line, int size)
 {
 	return( readline_Fifo((Fifo*) in->self,line,size) );
 }
